  "notes": "Cash-basis county. Governmental receipts, disbursements, transfers and balances from the Total Governmental Funds column of the Statement of Cash Receipts, Disbursements, and Changes in Fund Balances - Governmental Funds (p4, added by the v8 re-trim; previously derived from the Statement of Activities, p2). Beginning cash = Fund Balances - Beginning 11,283,359 (p4; cash basis, fund balance is all cash and investments); ending cash = total assets 10,265,024 (p3), which already includes investments 3,199,944 (ending_investments is informational, not additional). Roll-forward: 11,283,359 + 16,823,470 - 17,841,805 + 2,838,815 - 2,838,815 = 10,265,024. The fund statement shows General Government 5,280,717 and Capital Outlay 3,294,860 versus 5,281,141 and 3,294,436 on the Statement of Activities (424 reclassified), and Charges for Services 776,362 versus 776,361 (rounding); fund statement figures used. Taxes 9,851,479 split by fund column (p4) and nonmajor combining pages: General 8,972,891 + Inheritance 600,520 + Visitor Promotion 239,009 (p10) + 911 Emergency Management 39,059 (p12); General Fund taxes not broken down, kept as taxes (unlabeled). Miscellaneous 449,107 split: Keno Lottery Fund 155,473 (p12) keno/lottery, remainder 293,634 other. Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position - Cash Basis (p1). Fund-level transfers also recorded in detail (General -2,640,682, Road +2,554,682, Inheritance -179,999, Equipment Sinking +89,200, nonmajor net +176,799). Nonmajor budget schedule (p9) not recorded in detail since the combining statement (pp10-13) is more detailed; nonmajor recorded with Total column (13 funds). General Fund detail is by department (no object breakdown printed), so recorded as not itemized. Major fund schedules show only fund totals for disbursements. Nonmajor Miscellaneous 164,368 split by fund column in detail: Keno Lottery 155,473 keno/lottery; the other 8,895 miscellaneous. Read pages 1-13 of 13 Inheritance (247,840), ARP